//  Shared chat-bubble BACKING sheet. Four 64x32 cells.
//
//  one, two, three        the backing at one, two and three icon slots wide
//  blank                  deliberately empty -- the "none" bubble state
//
//  WHY EVERY CELL IS THE SAME SIZE WHEN THE BUBBLES ARE NOT
//
//  A .frames file carries ONE frameGrid, so every frame is 64x32 whether the
//  bubble drawn inside it is 26 wide or 62. Each backing is drawn CENTRED in
//  its cell, which means the part can be "centered" : true with a single fixed
//  offset and the backing grows symmetrically about the unit's centre line as
//  slots are added. Sizing the cells to the art instead would need a per-state
//  offset on the backing as well as on the icons, for no gain.
//
//  GEOMETRY, AND IT IS LOAD-BEARING -- the icon slot offsets in every chassis
//  .animation are derived from these numbers, not chosen independently.
//
//    8 pixels to the tile.
//    Icon cell 16px. Gap between icons 2px. Padding 4px. Border 1px.
//    one   = 1*16          + 8 + 2 = 26 wide
//    two   = 2*16 + 1*2    + 8 + 2 = 44 wide
//    three = 3*16 + 2*2    + 8 + 2 = 62 wide
//    Body 26 tall, tail 5 more. Body centre sits 3px above the cell centre,
//    which is where the 0.375 tile lift on every icon offset comes from.
//
//  PLACEHOLDER. Flat fill, one border colour, no chassis variation. The shape
//  and the measurements are the part worth keeping.

{
	"frameGrid" : {
		"size" : [64, 32],
		"dimensions" : [4, 1],
		"names" : [
			[ "one", "two", "three", "blank" ]
		]
	}
}
